      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Some additional information:\n1. Position sync not working:\n - Gameobject with Rigidbody (Non-Kinematic, gravity enabled)\n - 1 UdonBehaviour with Sync Position enabled\n - No transfer ownership on collision \n2. very unreliable variable synching:\nParent gameobject:\n  - with Rigidbody (Non-Kinematic, gravity enabled) \n  - 1 UdonBehaviour with Sync Position disabled\n  - No transfer ownership on collision \nChild gameobject:\n - No Rigidbody\n - 1 UdonBehaviour with UdonSynced(None) variables",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-04-21T02:43:23.093Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Position sync issues with UDON\nDemonstration: https://youtu.be/3W_P2mkOXfU\nWe were only two players in the world and despite not that many values being synced by the aircraft it barely updated on non-owning clients.\nScene setup:\n- created with UdonSharp by Merlin\n- around 40 UdonBehaviours in the scene\n- 1 of them is syncing the aircraft position/orientation/velocities (the position sync tickbox is ticked)\n- 1 float, 2 Vector3 and 1 Quaternion are being synced using the UdonSynced Attribute\n- the float variable and one vector are changing every frame and should be synced to other players together with the position data of the aircraft (handled by the tickboxed UdonBehaviour)\nWorld link: https://vrchat.com/i/boat-angussugar-87abc\nOutput Log can be made available if required.\n\nAnother case: very unreliable variable synching. The order of receiving packets is far from IN order: https://twitter.com/GuriboVR/status/1253421812450332676",
